; bfsodium HMAC_DRBG_SHA_256 : NIST SP 800_90A section 10 1 2
;
; HAND WRITTEN skeleton; The pseudorandom function is sha256/hmac  PASTED  and
; entered once per call of the standard's own HMAC underscore DRBG underscore
; Update and once per block of output;
;
; As in sha256/hashcore  a run of ONE repeated token is a repetition rather
; than a decision and is written as such; every offset and every branch below
; was worked out from the map and written down;
;
; IO  in:  seedlen{2} LE  ngen{2} LE  dklen{2} LE  seedbuf{256}
;     out: the LAST generate's dklen bytes
;
; Only the first seedlen bytes of the seed buffer are looked at; the rest MUST
; be nought;
;
; THE SEED IS ONE BLOB; the standard's seed material is the entropy input then
; the nonce then the personalisation string  and this routine takes the three
; already run together  because the standard concatenates them and never looks
; at the seam  and because a routine that took them apart would be asserting
; three lengths it has no use for;
;
; NGEN GENERATES HAPPEN AND THE LAST ONE IS WRITTEN OUT; that is CAVP's own
; shape  which instantiates  generates once and throws it away  then generates
; again and compares; the ones before the last still have to HAPPEN  because
; each advances the state  so they are made and not written;
;
; TWO PASTES OF HMAC AND NOT SIX  which is the whole reason this file is
; shaped the way it is; a paste of sha256/hmac is about six and a half million
; bytes of brainfuck  and the standard's instantiate and one generate are ten
; calls  so writing them out would be sixty five million bytes; Instead EVERY
; CALL IS ONE OF TWO KINDS and both kinds live in loops:
;   a K step  whose message is V then a tag byte then perhaps the seed  and
;             whose answer replaces K
;   a V step  whose message is V alone  and whose answer replaces V
; Update is a K step and a V step  twice over when it has data; a generate is
; a run of V steps that are written out  and then one more K step and V step;
; So there are two loops and two pastes  which is what sha256/hkdf already
; carries;
;
; THE PAIR LOOP COUNTS DOWN FROM TWO AND THAT IS HOW THE HALVES TELL THEMSELVES
; APART; after the loop's own decrement the counter is one on the K step and
; nought on the V step  so a copy of it IS the flag  and no comparison is
; needed anywhere;
;
; SEEDLEN IS AT MOST A HUNDRED AND FIFTY NINE; the K step's message is V then
; the tag then the seed  which is thirty two plus one plus seedlen  and a
; hundred and ninety two is the most sha256/hmac takes from memory;
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x001  seedlen{2}  u16 LE
;   @0x002:0x003  ngen{2}     u16 LE  how many generates happen
;   @0x004:0x005  dklen{2}    u16 LE  how many bytes each one makes
;   @0x006:0x105  seedbuf{256} u8     the seed material  as given
;   @0x108:0x207  stemp{256}  u8      hands the seed back after a copy
;   @0x208:0x227  K{32}       u8      the standard's K; starts at nought
;   @0x228:0x247  V{32}       u8      the standard's V; starts at ones
;   @0x248:0x267  ktemp{32}   u8      hands K back after a copy
;   @0x268:0x287  vtemp{32}   u8      hands V back after a copy
;   @0x288:0x2a7  R{32}       u8      the mac  as a byte string  before it is
;                          routed to K or to V; ONE staging copy rather than
;                          two readers  so the eight word reversal is written
;                          once and not once per destination
;   @0x2a8:0x2c7  OUT{32}     u8      the block written out and spent
;   @0x2cc:0x2cd  dklen kept  to reset the count owed at each generate
;   @0x2ce:0x2cf  the count still owed in THIS generate
;   @0x2d0:0x2d5  chances flag test back and two spare cells
;   @0x2d6        the generates still to do
;   @0x2d7        the flag that says THIS generate is the one written out
;   @0x2d8        the pair counter  two then one then nought
;   @0x2d9        the half counter inside a pair
;   @0x2da        this call is the K step
;   @0x2db        the tag byte  nought on the first pair and one on the second
;   @0x2dc        the message carries the seed
;   @0x2dd        the first pass  which instantiates and makes no output
;   @0x2e0:0x9eb  sha256/hmac's frame  pasted at @0x2e0; footprint 0:1803
;
; A digest is a byte string and hmac leaves its answer as eight little endian
; words  so the copy into R reverses each word;

; read the three counts and the seed
,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
